"""
Builds the training "golden set": 10 prompts for each QC project template in
data/train_templates/ that passes QC validation (87 templates, 870 prompts).
Each template's main.py is the target answer.

Outputs
  data/train_prompts_src.txt   folder | segment | specificity | prompt
                               (the format finetune/build_dataset.py reads)
  data/train_prompts.jsonl     same rows in the data/prompts_100.jsonl schema

Prompt grid (same as the 100-prompt test set, see build_prompts.py):
  versions 1-9:  3 customer segments x 3 specificity levels
  version 10:    ceiling prompt, near-pseudocode description of the code

Segments:  individual (hobbyist vocabulary, single ticker, no constraints),
           startup (terse researcher shorthand, in a hurry),
           institutional (spec-style, risk limits, compliance, matching an
           internal implementation)
Specificity: vague (key parameters left out), precise (every parameter needed
           to reproduce the template), over_specified (precise plus requirements
           that do not change trading: plotting, naming, logging, comments),
           ceiling (near-pseudocode)

Prompt text follows each template's CODE, not its description or spec.
Vague prompts omit dates and cash on purpose; every other prompt states the
template's start date, end date and cash where the code sets them.

EXISTING holds the hand-written rows from the 2026-11-08 version of
train_prompts_src.txt (text unchanged except where a comment says so); they
fill their grid cell and the remaining cells are written here. The two
templates that fail QC validation (alternative-data,
alternative-data-chain-universe-eodhdupcomingdividends) get no new prompts.

Templates: https://github.com/QuantConnect/Documentation/tree/master/project-templates
(Apache 2.0). Never use data/templates/ (the 10 test templates) here.
"""
import json
from pathlib import Path

GRID = [
    ("individual", "vague"), ("individual", "precise"), ("individual", "over_specified"),
    ("startup", "vague"), ("startup", "precise"), ("startup", "over_specified"),
    ("institutional", "vague"), ("institutional", "precise"), ("institutional", "over_specified"),
    ("reference", "ceiling"),
]

EXCLUDED = {"alternative-data", "alternative-data-chain-universe-eodhdupcomingdividends"}

